THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

Paralome depends on the following packages, which are installed separately and
are not distributed as part of this software. Their own licences apply to them.

    numpy, scipy, pandas, scikit-learn, matplotlib   BSD
    statsmodels                                      BSD
    plotly                                           MIT
    openpyxl                                         MIT
    pysam                                            MIT
    typer, click                                     MIT
    MOODS-python                                     dual: GPL-3 or Biopython

MOODS-python is taken under the Biopython licence arm, not the GPL-3 arm. This
is deliberate and load-bearing: taking it under GPL-3 would impose copyleft
obligations on Paralome as a whole and would make a separate commercial licence
impossible to offer.

The single-cell analyses invoke R (Seurat, Signac, Matrix) as a separate
process through Rscript. Those packages are MIT licensed, are installed by the
user into their own R library, and are not distributed with Paralome.

